   "unmapped": [
    "Two-sided matching market: N players (learners) and K >= N arms; arms have known fixed preferences over players and resolve collisions by accepting their most preferred proposing player (rejected players get reward 0)",
    "Serial dictatorship: all arms share the same preference ranking over players, giving a unique stable matching",
    "Regret per player is stable regret, measured against the player's stable-matched arm rather than its best arm",
    "Players observe the full matching result each round (decentralized, collision-based communication)",
    "All players' preferences are distinct"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "If player $p_i$ is successfully matched, it will receive a random reward $X_i(t)$, which is 1-subgaussian with mean $\\mu_{i,\\bar{A}_i(t)}$. If player $p_i$ is rejected, it will receive $X_i(t) = 0$. ... We consider the market satisfies serial dictatorship, where each arm shares the same preference. ... $R_i(T) = \\sum_{t=1}^T \\mu_{i,m^\\ast(i)} - \\EE{\\sum_{t=1}^{T}X_i(T)}$"
  }
